.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-input\fP=\fIfile\fP {\fB\-I\fP\fIfile\fP}
.br
The swath file to open. For Kongsberg data either the *.kmwcd or the *.kmall,
or the *.wcd or the *.all, of a survey line; the other file is found as described above.
For Reson 7k data the *.s7k file. The file name may also be given as the last argument.
.TP
.B \-\-format\fP=\fIformat_id\fP {\fB\-F\fP\fIformat_id\fP}
.br
The MBIO format of the input file. By default it is taken from the file name;
*.kmwcd files are read as format 261, *.wcd files as format 58 and *.s7k files
as format 89.
.TP
.B \-\-ping\fP=\fIindex\fP {\fB\-P\fP\fIindex\fP}
.br
The water column ping (counted from 0) shown first, exported or summarized.
Default: 0.
.TP
.B \-\-swath\fP=\fIindex\fP {\fB\-S\fP\fIindex\fP}
.br
With \fB\-\-export\fP, the swath of the ping (0 is the aftmost swath in multiple
swath modes). Default: the first swath.
.TP
.B \-\-bottom
With \fB\-\-export\fP, draw the soundings of the matching survey ping.
.TP
.B \-\-wc-bottom
With \fB\-\-export\fP, draw the bottom detections recorded in the water column.
.TP
.B \-\-straight
With \fB\-\-export\fP, use straight rays instead of ray tracing.
.TP
.B \-\-export\fP=\fIimage.png\fP
.br
Write an image of one swath (PNG or JPEG by the file name) and exit without
opening a window.
.TP
.B \-\-size\fP=\fIwidth\fPx\fIheight\fP
.br
The size in pixels of the exported image. Default: 1400x900.
.TP
.B \-\-dump
Print a summary of the survey line and exit: the files found, the numbers of
pings, matched pings and position records, the amplitude range and fill value,
the longest slant range and the top of the default depth window,
the position, speed, course, heading and transducer depth (interpolated for a water
column ping without a survey ping) at the ping given by \fB\-\-ping\fP, and the
depth ratio and across track difference between the bottom detections of the
water column and the soundings, for straight and for ray traced geometry, over every
tenth water column ping. Each beam's detection is compared with the sounding (not
null) whose two-way travel time (from \fBmb_ttimes\fP, see \fBmbio\fP(3)) is
nearest to its own among those seen within 10 degrees of its direction in straight
geometry: the detection recorded with the water column is the sonar's own detection
of the beam, so its travel time finds the beam's sounding however the soundings are
ordered (extra and multiple detections, several receive fans, lost water column
datagrams) and positioned. Of several soundings as near in time, where the ping gives
its detections in fractions of a sample (Kongsberg *.kmall, Reson 7k), within the
float precision of the travel times, the one nearest in direction is taken; where it
gives them in whole samples (*.all and *.wcd, *.kmall water column datagrams of
version 0), within a sample, the one whose beam angle (\fBmb_ttimes\fP) is nearest
to the beam's own, unless the ping's beam angles disagree with those of the water
column by more than half the beam spacing (as MBIO's for *.kmall, computed with the
roll at the echo, can), and then again the one nearest in direction. The summary
says how many beams were compared each way. The same pairs serve both geometries.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose {\fB\-V\fP}
Print the program name and version, and with \fB\-\-export\fP what was written.
.TP
.B \-\-help {\fB\-H\fP}
Print the usage message and exit.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MB_RENDERER
Set to \fBlegacy-gl\fP to draw with OpenGL instead of QRhi, where
\fBmbwcdview\fP was built with both (\fB\-DbuildQt6LegacyGL=ON\fP, the default
except on macOS).

.SH EXAMPLES
To view a Kongsberg survey line, open either of its files:
.br
	mbwcdview 0080_20250618_223434.kmwcd
.br

To write an image of ping 100 with the soundings and the water column bottom
detections:
.br
	mbwcdview \-I 0030_20250208_100905.kmall \-\-ping=100 \-\-bottom \-\-wc-bottom \-\-export=ping100.png
.br

To check the pairing of the files and the ray tracing of a line:
.br
	mbwcdview \-\-dump \-I 0030_20250208_100905.kmall
.br

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmbsystem\fP(1), \fBmbinfo\fP(1), \fBmbprocess\fP(1), \fBmbio\fP(3)

.SH BUGS
The soundings of a ping are assigned to the swaths by splitting them into equal
blocks, which is right for dual swath data with one receiver; when the receive
fans have different numbers of soundings all soundings of the ping are drawn on
each swath. Water column data stored inside *.kmall files are not read. Dual head
and dual receiver systems, and water column data of EM 2040 scanning mode, have not
been tested.
